54. 559.375 Td
(The statutory architecture of 18 U.S.C. § 2331 establishes a functional distinction between international terrorism under) Tj
T* (subsection \(1\) and domestic terrorism under subsection \(5\). While both definitions share identical core prongs regarding) Tj
T* (the appearance of intent—intimidating civilians, influencing policy, or affecting government conduct through mass) Tj
T* (destruction, assassination, or kidnapping—they bifurcate on territorial jurisdiction and executive designation authorities.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0. g
54. 505.375 Td
(Under international terrorism provisions, the executive branch leverages designation authority under Section 219 of the) Tj
T* (Immigration and Nationality Act \(8 U.S.C. § 1189\) and Executive Order 13224 to issue binding Foreign Terrorist) Tj
T* (Organization \(FTO\) and Specially Designated Global Terrorist \(SDGT\) lists. These designations trigger strict liability) Tj
T* (criminal material support prohibitions under 18 U.S.C. § 2339B, which withstand constitutional challenge because) Tj
T* (foreign entities operating abroad do not possess First Amendment rights \(Holder v. Humanitarian Law Project, 2010\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0. g
54. 439.375 Td
(Conversely, domestic terrorism under 18 U.S.C. § 2331\(5\) functions primarily as an investigatory classification, a) Tj
T* (sentencing enhancement factor under U.S.S.G. § 3A1.4, or a jurisdictional threshold for specific investigative authorities) Tj
T* (under the Attorney General's Guidelines for Domestic FBI Operations. It does not create a standalone substantive) Tj
T* (federal crime for purely domestic acts absent an independent federal violent offense, such as acts involving weapons of) Tj
T* (mass destruction under 18 U.S.C. § 2332a or acts of terrorism transcending national boundaries under 18 U.S.C. §) Tj
T* (2332b.) Tj
ET
