54. 720. Td
(The Court rejected the argument advanced by Florida and Texas that large social media networks function as common) Tj
T* (carriers stripped of First Amendment rights. The majority opinion clarified that state regulations compelling platforms to) Tj
T* (host speech contrary to their internal community standards impermissibly alter the expressive compilation of the) Tj
T* (platform.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0. g
54. 666. Td
(Simultaneously, statutory platform governance in the United States is anchored by Section 230 of the Communications) Tj
T* (Decency Act of 1996 \(47 U.S.C. § 230\). Under 47 U.S.C. § 230\(c\)\(1\), interactive computer services are shielded from) Tj
T* (being treated as the publisher or speaker of information provided by third-party content creators, neutralizing) Tj
T* (common-law publisher liability for torts, defamation, or civil harms stemming from hosted user content. Complementing) Tj
T* (this protection, 47 U.S.C. § 230\(c\)\(2\)\(A\) immunizes platforms from civil liability for voluntary actions taken in good faith) Tj
T* (to restrict access to, or availability of, material considered obscene, lewd, lascivious, filthy, excessively violent,) Tj
T* (harassing, or otherwise objectionable, whether or not such material is constitutionally protected.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0. g
54. 576. Td
(This statutory and constitutional structure allows private platforms to enforce proactive harm thresholds on domestic) Tj
T* (political rhetoric that the state is constitutionally forbidden to censor. Platforms routinely deplatform domestic extremist) Tj
T* (groups, remove sovereign citizen manifestos, suppress election-denial movements that carry latent threats of violence,) Tj
T* (and restrict hate speech without demonstrating imminent lawless action under Brandenburg. While the state must prove) Tj
T* (an act dangerous to human life and establish specific intent to coerce under 18 U.S.C. § 2331\(5\), private platforms take) Tj
T* (proactive action based on corporate terms of service and internal risk management policies.) Tj
ET
